---
date added: 2026-11-11
title: Bacon, Broccoli & Gruyère Potato Crust Quiche
author: Katie Bien
source: https://www.instagram.com/reel/DfK8GKsPIL8/
tags: breakfast, quiche, potatoes, bacon, broccoli, holiday, thanksgiving
cook time: 1 hour 5 minutes
notes: This is what I would make on Thanksgiving morning! A crispy potato crust filled with fluffy eggs, crispy bacon, broccoli, and the perfect combination of Gruyère and sharp cheddar. It's hearty, delicious, and perfect for a holiday breakfast!
---

Peel your @medium russet or golden potatoes{6}(amount will vary depending on size) and cut them into smaller pieces. Add to a #pot{} of boiling water and cook until fork tender.

Drain the potatoes and refrigerate until completely cooled.

Spray a #springform pan{} with @avocado oil spray{}. Press the cooled potatoes into the bottom and up the sides of the pan to form your crust. I like using the bottom of a cup sprayed with a little avocado oil to prevent sticking and help press and shape the crust evenly.

Spray the crust with a little more avocado oil and sprinkle with @salt{}.

Bake at 425°F for ~{20-25%minutes} to pre-bake the crust until lightly golden and starting to crisp.

In a #bowl{}, whisk together @eggs{6}, @ricotta{1/2%cup}, @bacon{5%slices}(cooked and diced), @broccoli{1%cup}(cooked, diced), @shredded cheese{1 heaping%cup}(1/2 Gruyère, 1/2 sharp cheddar), @salt{} and @pepper{} until combined.

Pour the egg mixture into your pre-baked potato crust and top with @additional shredded cheddar{}.

Bake at 425°F for ~{40-45%minutes}, or until the quiche is fully set and no longer jiggly in the center.

Let cool slightly before removing from the springform pan. Finish with the extra @bacon{2%slices}(cooked and crumbled), @fresh chives{} and @flaky salt{}.
